## 2. Definitions

**You** means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

**Organization** means a company, partnership, institution, government body, nonprofit organization, or other legal or organizational entity on whose behalf You exercise rights under this License. Personal activity is not activity on behalf of an Organization solely because You are employed by or affiliated with it.

**Trial Use** means exercising the source inspection permissions in Section 4.1 or compiling, running, modifying, or deploying the Licensed Software under Section 4.2 for Your own personal use or an Organization's internal use, including evaluation, testing, and actual internal workflows. All Trial Use is subject to the applicable Trial Period.

**Trial Period** means a single period of 30 consecutive calendar days. For personal use, it begins on the date You first exercise a permission granted by Section 4.1 or Section 4.2, including source inspection or copying under Section 4.1. For use on behalf of an Organization, one shared period begins on the date the first person does so on its behalf and applies to all of that Organization's users, copies, and instances. Sections 4.1 and 4.2 share this period; inspecting the source and later deploying it do not provide separate trials. Hosted Service use under Section 5 does not start this period. A new version, copy, fork, installation, account, device, deployment, or user does not restart or extend it.

**Production Use** means any use of the Licensed Software for an actual business, organizational, operational, customer-facing, revenue-generating, monitoring, analytics, development workflow, or other ongoing purpose beyond Trial Use.

Production Use includes internal use that provides operational or business value even when the Licensed Software is not exposed to external customers.

**Client Components** means the hook scripts, skill files, and settings snippets that the Licensor provides for installation on a user's machine or inside a skill to send ratings, comments, and session data to a RateXp service. They also include browser code delivered by the Hosted Service as needed to access and use that service. Client Components do not include the RateXp server software.

**Hosted Service** means a RateXp service operated by the Licensor, such as https://ratexp-app.azurewebsites.net and https://ratexp-core.azurewebsites.net.

**Commercial License** means a separate written license agreement issued by the Licensor permitting uses not allowed by this License.

