## 4. Permitted Use

### 4.1 Source Inspection Trial License

Under this License, You receive a limited, royalty-free license to access, inspect, review, and make private copies of the source code for inspection and review only during the applicable Trial Period, subject to Sections 7 and 8. Copies must remain on devices or private infrastructure controlled by You or the Organization on whose behalf You act. These permissions are part of the 30-day trial license and do not grant continuing source access or use rights after that period.

When the Trial Period ends, the permissions granted by this Section expire. You must obtain a Commercial License from the Licensor before continuing to exercise them. This expiry is subject to the independent rights preserved in Section 18.

You may not publish or mirror the source code, or provide it to third parties, without the Licensor's prior written permission, except for the limited internal access allowed by Section 8 and the independent rights preserved in Section 18. Compiling, executing, or modifying the Licensed Software, or operating a RateXp service, requires permission under Section 4.2, Section 5, or a Commercial License.

### 4.2 Local and Organizational Trial

Under the trial license granted by this License, You may compile, run, modify, and deploy the Licensed Software only if all of the following conditions are satisfied:

1. These activities are solely Trial Use within the applicable Trial Period. Personal use and actual internal organizational workflows, including data ingestion, are permitted during that period.
2. The Licensed Software runs on infrastructure controlled by You or the Organization on whose behalf You act. Local devices, virtual machines, containers, company servers, shared internal environments, and cloud deployments are permitted.
3. Access to the running software is limited to You for personal use or to the Organization's employees and contractors acting on its behalf for internal use. Multiple users and devices may participate, and network access between them is permitted.
4. All users and instances acting on behalf of the same Organization share its single Trial Period. Adding users, moving to another server, or creating another instance does not provide another trial.
5. The Licensed Software is not offered to third parties as a product or service, or incorporated into a product or service supplied to third parties.
6. Copies and modifications remain private, and all access and use comply with Sections 7 and 8. The trial does not grant permission for public redistribution, competitive use, or AI model training prohibited by those Sections.

When the Trial Period ends, You and the Organization must stop compiling, running, modifying, and deploying the Licensed Software under this Section, including ingesting data into those instances and using its Client Components with them, unless a Commercial License permitting continued use is already in effect. The source inspection permissions in Section 4.1 expire at the same time. Use of the Licensor's Hosted Service under Section 5 remains permitted, and the independent rights preserved in Section 18 remain unaffected.

## 5. Hosted Service and Clients

The trial limits in Sections 4.1, 4.2, and 6 do not apply to the permissions expressly granted in this Section. Under this License, without a trial time limit and for any number of people within any Organization, You may:

1. access and use the Hosted Service, including its dashboard, and submit ratings, comments, session data, and other supported data for personal or organizational purposes, subject to the service terms described below;
2. download, install, privately copy, and run the Client Components as needed to access and use the Hosted Service, including during normal organizational workflows; and
3. make private changes to the Client Components needed for installation or configuration for Your own use or the Organization's internal use, subject to Sections 7 and 8.

The Client Components must retain applicable copyright and license notices. Publishing, redistributing, or bundling them in packages supplied to third parties requires the Licensor's prior written permission under Section 8. You may instead share links to the Licensor's official downloads. Internal installation for authorized users under this Section remains permitted.

Client Components used under this Section may connect only to the Hosted Service. Using them to connect to another RateXp service requires permission under Section 4.2 or a Commercial License.

Data submission to the Hosted Service is free of charge and has no data-volume limit or trial time limit under this License. This permission applies to both individuals and Organizations, including normal organizational workflows. Access to and use of the Hosted Service, including data submission, are subject to its available capacity.

The Licensor's [Terms of Service](./TERMS.md) govern account requirements, privacy, acceptable use, and service operation. They do not change the free data-submission permission granted by this Section. This License does not guarantee continuous service availability.

Deploying or operating another instance of the RateXp server software is governed by Section 4.2 or a Commercial License. Using the Hosted Service does not start, extend, or restart the period permitted for that separate instance.

