## 7. Use Restrictions

The restrictions in this Section apply to the permissions in Sections 4 and 5, including during the Trial Period, subject to the independent rights preserved in Section 18.

### 7.1 No Circumvention

You may not divide an Organization into teams, departments, subsidiaries, accounts, environments, machines, or individual users for the purpose of avoiding the limitations of this License.

Affiliated entities under common control will be treated as one Organization where they coordinate their use of the Licensed Software. Control means the power to direct an entity's management or policies, directly or indirectly, through ownership, voting rights, contract, or otherwise.

### 7.2 Competitive Use

Without the Licensor's prior written permission, You may not use the Licensed Software, its source code, or modified versions to develop, train, improve, operate, or provide a product or service that substantially reproduces RateXp's core functionality or competes with RateXp.

Private modifications and internal instances used solely as permitted by Section 4 are allowed and are not, by themselves, prohibited competitive use. This allowance does not authorize using them to develop or support a separate competing product or service. This restriction concerns use of the Licensed Software or its source code; it does not prohibit independent development without such use, subject to any intellectual property rights that apply independently of this License.

### 7.3 AI and Machine Learning Training

Without the Licensor's prior written permission, You may not use the source code of the Licensed Software, including modified versions or portions of that source code, as training data for machine learning or artificial intelligence models. This restriction includes pretraining, fine-tuning, and further training of existing models, as well as supplying the source code for those purposes or authorizing others to use it for those purposes.

To the extent applicable law permits a rights reservation, the Licensor expressly reserves rights to reproduce or extract that source code for text and data mining for such training purposes. No such permission is granted by this License. Mandatory exceptions preserved by Section 18 remain unaffected.

