After You receive Your first written notice of a violation from the Licensor, Your rights are automatically reinstated once You are in full compliance and have taken practical steps to correct past violations, provided both conditions are met no later than 30 calendar days after receiving that notice. If both conditions are already met when You receive that notice, reinstatement takes effect on receipt. Your rights remain terminated until reinstatement. A later notice of a violation does not give You another automatic right to reinstatement.

Upon termination, You must cease exercising the rights granted by this License, including running the Licensed Software under it, unless and until those rights are reinstated or separately granted in writing by the Licensor.

Reinstatement does not restart or extend a Trial Period, authorize a use requiring a Commercial License, or waive any claim arising from a past violation. Access to the Hosted Service itself remains governed by its [Terms of Service](./TERMS.md).

Termination under this License does not prevent the Licensor from granting You rights under a separate Commercial License.

